[Music]  respawn has released the first official  trailer and details for apex legends  season six boosted so let's dive into  what we know  season six's new playable legend is  rampart we get our first look at the  character in the season six cinematic  launch trailer as well as hints as to  what her abilities are  keep in mind that respawn hasn't  officially confirmed rampart's abilities  yet so this  next portion is a little bit of  guesswork don't take it as fact  rampart seems to be a defender whose  abilities help her squad lock down his  own  about halfway through the trailer we see  bangalore shooting through a laser wall  though bangalore's bullets pass through  the wall the bullet shot out or don't  in fact taking it a step further it  looks like bangalore's shots are being  amplified as they pass through the  shield  if we were to hazard a guess we think  this is rampart's tactical ability  some form of makeshift cover that helps  her and her squad mates better defend  his own  it looks a lot like the a wall a pilot  ability from titanfall 2.  sheila rampart's turret is likely her  ultimate ability  nothing quite says i'm defending this  zone like a massive chain gun  sheila might be our hint at what  rampart's passive ability is as well  especially when you consider the  character's history as an expert modder  as the trailer zooms in on rampart  firing sheila you can see a red dot  laser sight on the gun  now maybe sheila just comes with that  sight however this could also be hinting  towards rampart having a passive ability  that she mods all her weapons with the  laser sight to make it easier to aim  weapons from the hip  that would make it far easier to spray  assault rifles lmgs and smgs at an  attacking team speaking of smgs a  familiar one is coming to apex legends  in season six  respawn has confirmed that season 6's  new weapon is the volt  a fan favorite smg from titanfall 2. the  gun wasn't featured in the new trailer  so we still don't know whether it will  behave like it did in titanfall 2.  however respawn describes the volt as a  shocking new weapon which may hint that  it naturally fires disrupter rounds a  hop-up attachment that was removed from  apex legends at the start of season 3.  when season 6 launches rampart won't be  the only legend who joins the apex games  with a sense of style and knack for  crafting gadgets  season 6 adds a new crafting feature to  the game though how it will work remains  a bit  unclear respawn writes that players will  be able to find materials and craft  better gear  whether that means improving the gear  you already have or building brand new  items  hasn't been clarified in terms of the  sense of style  apex legends is getting sprays as teased  with the graffiti that appeared on the  construction signs on world's edge  you'll be able to unlock brand new holo  sprays in season 6's battle pass that's  cool and all but we want to know how  these new sprays may impact gameplay  like  can bloodhound pick up someone's tracks  from the hollow spray they leave behind  oh and speaking of those construction  signs we finally get to see what at  least some of them are for  the opening shot of the cinematic  trailer shows a rocket launch pad that's  been built just outside the dome which  is where you can currently find a  collection of construction signs the  trailer doesn't showcase what the  construction signs around drill site are  for though  now where could that rocket be going  well if you've been following the quest  storyline  for season 5 then you know the apex  games are heading to olympus a city on  the home planet of octane and lifeline  the legends are going to need some form  of transportation to get there  and perhaps this rocket is just that new  planet means a new location but respawn  hasn't confirmed whether that means a  brand new map or just  places to visit in quest come the start  of season 6. we may get a hint at season  6's quest and who trusts who  in the final shot of the trailer as well  it shows most of the legends meeting  rampart but there are a few noticeable  absentees  both revenant and loba aren't there for  instance which might hint towards how  the two are now off on their own trying  to find a way to kill  revenant caustic is absent as well which  may be in reference to his role as a  traitor in season five's quest storyline  maybe the other legends don't want to  hang out with him anymore watson is also  curiously absent though this could be  because she's still struggling to come  to terms with being betrayed in season  5. blood owned isn't there either though  as seen in an apex legends comic the  tracker excused themselves from the  group following the legends turning on  one another and not trusting each other  so perhaps bloodhound is just wary of  working with the others again  season 6 boosted is scheduled to begin  on august 18th we'll be sure to cover  the new season in full as additional  details are revealed  [Music]  you

